{"ts": 1789777319.2857301, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "This confirms my concern. Adding a *random* third feature to the 17+29 pair gives ~0.82\u20130.90 \u2014 mechanically above the pair's 0.943? No: it's mostly *below* 0.943. The third feature dilutes the two strong signals by averaging in a weak one, and the \"gain\" to 1.014 for feature 13 is the upper tail of ~20 noisy draws around a baseline of ~0.87.\n\nThe diagnostic on feature 13 is decisive: flipping its sign drops 17+13 from 0.799 to 0.218 and 29+13 from 0.732 to 0.144. So feature 13 does carry some real directional signal. But its standalone 0.414 has SE\u22480.22, so the true value is plausibly ~0.15\u20130.25 after shrinkage, and its marginal contribution to an already-strong pair is smaller still.\n\nLet me make a decision between the pair and the triple."}
