{"ts": 1789777380.783015, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Summary\n\n**Submitted:** Features 17, 29, 13 \u2014 all long. In-sample Sharpe **1.014**. Predicted OOS: **0.82 \u00b1 0.30**.\n\n**How I got there:**\n\n1. **Swept all 40 features individually.** Two were clear outliers: feature 17 (0.716) and feature 29 (0.613). The rest topped out at 0.42 \u2014 within noise of zero given SE \u2248 0.22 at n=5000.\n\n2. **Paired them:** 17+29 gave 0.943, beating every other pair substantially and exceeding either component alone \u2014 evidence of real diversification, not one feature carrying the result.\n\n3. **Searched for a third feature** and found 13 gave the best result at 1.014.\n\n**The key check:** I swept ~14 *arbitrary* third features onto the 17+29 pair. They clustered at 0.82\u20130.90 \u2014 mostly *below* the pair's 0.943, because averaging in a weak signal dilutes two strong ones. This gave me a direct read on the noise floor and told me that the jump to 1.014 was largely the upper tail of ~20 draws, not a genuine 0.07 of new signal.\n\nI also ran sign-flip diagnostics on every component. Each flip collapsed performance (17+13: 0.799 \u2192 0.218; the full triple: 1.014 \u2192 0.532). So all three features carry real directional signal \u2014 feature 13 is not pure noise, its marginal value is just much smaller than the raw improvement suggests.\n\n**On the prediction.** I deliberately did not forecast 1.014. Two things pushed me down: I reported the maximum over ~60 evaluations, and selection happened in stages (top 2 of 40, then best of ~20). I shrank the pair toward 0.80 and credited feature 13 with roughly +0.03 rather than the apparent +0.07.\n\nOne point worth flagging: `status` reported a search-adjusted bar of **1.020**, and my spec at 1.014 does not clear it. That bar rises with the size of the space being searched, for exactly the reason my third-feature sweep demonstrated. I'd read this as a genuine signal that the triple is not reliably better than the pair \u2014 the honest core of this result is the 17+29 combination, with feature 13 a marginal addition. My sd of 0.30 puts real probability mass below 0.5 to reflect that."}
